#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD0041 expect=skipped domain=CM
#note "Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner, verdict 2-1'): --PRESP moved from the authored `not var_exists(\"--PRESP\") or` disjunct to Requirements.Variables.All. The dataset carries no CMPRESP column at all, so the rule SKIPS; FDA-SD1147 reports the absent --PRESP once for the dataset (--OCCUR present). Before the round the two populated CMOCCUR rows fired, one finding per record for one dataset fact - this file pinned that as a violation."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset CM class=INTERVENTIONS label="Concomitant Medications"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col CMSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col CMTRT   type=Char label="Reported Name of Drug, Med, or Therapy"
col CMOCCUR type=Char label="Occurrence"
---
S1 | CM | 001 | 1 | ASPIRIN   | Y
S1 | CM | 001 | 2 | IBUPROFEN | N
S1 | CM | 001 | 3 | PARACETAM |
